[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=Power Shutdown Confirmation Page Manager\\For 4-Series (and 3-Series)||1
  Cmn2=processors.\\\\When an automatic shutdown sequence is initiated,||1
  Cmn3=this module asserts a warning\\page and runs a countdown (analog,||1
  Cmn4=serial, or both). The touchpanel page typically\\shows a "system||1
  Cmn5=is about to shut down" message plus Cancel and Confirm buttons.\\
  Cmn6=\\Typical flow:\\1. Pulse [D]Initiate when the auto-shutdown sequence||1
  Cmn7=begins.\\2. [D]Warning_Page_FB goes high — join this to your confirmation||1
  Cmn8=page / subpage.\\3. [S]Serial_Count_FB and/or [A]Analog_Count_FB||1
  Cmn9=drive the on-screen timer.\\4. User presses Cancel  ? page de-asserts,||1
  Cmn10=timer resets for next time, no shutdown.\\5. User presses Confirm||1
  Cmn11=? [D]Shutdown_OS pulses, page de-asserts, timer resets.\\6. Timer||1
  Cmn12=reaches 0     ? same as Confirm (auto-shutdown).\\\\Inputs:\\[D]Initiate||1
  Cmn13=- starts the shutdown warning sequence (asserts page + countdown)\\
  Cmn14=[D]Cancel - de-asserts the warning page and resets the counter (no||1
  Cmn15=shutdown)\\[D]Confirm - pulses Shutdown_OS, de-asserts the warning||1
  Cmn16=page, resets the counter\\[A]Time_Override - optional; sets countdown||1
  Cmn17=length in seconds (1d..65535d)\\\\Outputs:\\[D]Warning_Page_FB -
  Cmn18=||1high while the confirmation page is shown (countdown is running)\\
  Cmn19=[D]Shutdown_OS - 1 ms pulse on Confirm or when the countdown expires\\
  Cmn20=[S]Serial_Count_FB - time remaining, format set by String_Format||1
  Cmn21=parameter\\[A]Analog_Count_FB - whole seconds remaining\\\\Parameters:
  Cmn22=\\[I]Countdown_Time - default countdown length in seconds (1s..600s;\\
  Cmn23=||Duse [A]Time_Override for longer durations)\\
  Cmn24=[I]String_Format - serial time display format:\\    1d = Minimal||1
  Cmn25=length [42]\\    2d = Always show minutes [0:42]\\    3d = Always||1
  Cmn26=show hours and minutes [0:00:42]\\    4d = Always show minutes with||1
  Cmn27=leading zeros [00:42]\\    5d = Always show hours and minutes with||1
  Cmn28=leading zeros [00:00:42]\\\\SIMPL Windows tips:\\- Drive the confirmation||1
  Cmn29=page visibility from Warning_Page_FB.\\- Wire Cancel / Confirm button||1
  Cmn30=presses to Cancel / Confirm.\\- Wire Shutdown_OS into your actual||1
  Cmn31=power-down / system-off logic.\\- Put static warning text on the||1
  Cmn32=VTPro page (or a separate serial join).\\\\-- VERSION HISTORY --
  Cmn33=\\v1.0  2026-07-15\\- Repurposed from Serial/Analog Countdown v2.
  Cmn34=0 (Robert G Walker)\\- Geared specifically to power shutdown confirmation||1
  Cmn35=UX\\
[END]
